Validate the `url` parameter to ensure it is a valid and safe URL. Consider using a whitelist of allowed domains or a URL parsing library to check the format and content of the URL before making the request. Example:

```java
private static final Set<String> ALLOWED_DOMAINS = Set.of("example.com", "another-example.com");

@GetMapping("/api/preview")
public ResponseEntity<String> preview(@RequestParam String url) {
    if (!isValidUrl(url)) {
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body("Invalid URL");
    }
    String html = http.get().uri(url).retrieve().body(String.class);
    String title = extractTitle(html);
    return ResponseEntity.ok(title);
}

private boolean isValidUrl(String url) {
    try {
        URI uri = new URI(url);
        String host = uri.getHost();
        if (host == null || !ALLOWED_DOMAINS.contains(host)) {
            return false;
        }
        return true;
    } catch (URISyntaxException e) {
        return false;
    }
}
```

Consider adding more robust error handling and logging to improve the method's reliability and maintainability. For example:

```java
@GetMapping("/diagnostics/ping")
public String ping(@RequestParam String host) {
    try {
        ProcessBuilder pb = new ProcessBuilder("sh", "-c", "ping -c 1 " + host);
        Process process = pb.start();
        int exit = process.waitFor();
        return exit == 0 ? "reachable" : "unreachable";
    } catch (IOException | InterruptedException e) {
        // Log the exception and return a meaningful error message
        return "error: " + e.getMessage();
    }
}
```

Use a JOIN query to fetch all order items for the day in a single query. For example:

```java
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public List<OrderSummary> summaries(LocalDate day) {
    List<Order> dayOrders = orders.findByCreatedDate(day);
    List<OrderItem> allItems = items.findByOrderIds(dayOrders.stream().map(Order::getId).collect(Collectors.toList()));
    Map<Long, List<OrderItem>> orderItemsMap = allItems.stream().collect(Collectors.groupingBy(OrderItem::getOrderId));
    List<OrderSummary> result = new ArrayList<>();
    for (Order order : dayOrders) {
        List<OrderItem> lines = orderItemsMap.get(order.getId());
        BigDecimal total = lines.stream()
                .map(OrderItem::getPrice)
                .reduce(BigDecimal.ZERO, BigDecimal::add);
        result.add(new OrderSummary(order.getId(), lines.size(), total));
    }
    return result;
}
```

